WEBVTT

00:14.790 --> 00:16.660
Just accept it.

00:16.660 --> 00:21.750
I'm not about to let something of Uzal's into my home without knowing what's inside.

00:22.250 --> 00:24.500
Let's see what you've got in there.

00:32.550 --> 00:34.430
Wh-What happened!?

00:35.890 --> 00:37.430
That's enough of that.

00:37.430 --> 00:39.310
What are you doing here!?

00:39.310 --> 00:41.440
Nobody should be able to get in!

00:43.730 --> 00:47.690
N-Nene used Hacker mode, didn't she?

00:48.110 --> 00:49.400
But why!?

00:49.400 --> 00:52.070
This one isn't even your puppet!

00:52.570 --> 00:55.540
Clarin said she doesn't want you breaking BUER.

00:56.450 --> 01:00.210
I do thank thee, modestly-bosomed girls!

01:00.210 --> 01:03.960
I be ready and willing to respond to thy feelings!

01:04.090 --> 01:07.260
Uzal warned me not to take my eyes off you.

01:07.260 --> 01:10.090
She says destroying you is preferable to letting Korobase have you.

01:11.970 --> 01:13.640
Damn that Uzal.

01:13.640 --> 01:15.970
Her orders really piss me off sometimes.

03:08.630 --> 03:09.670
Clarin?

03:11.000 --> 03:12.960
Mind if we hold hands for a bit?

03:17.640 --> 03:21.220
Your application for an enrollment interview has been received and confirmed.

03:21.220 --> 03:23.060
Please proceed, applicant.

03:23.390 --> 03:25.350
My name is Nanakorobi Nene.

03:25.350 --> 03:27.150
Thank you for your time.

03:28.520 --> 03:31.900
Please relax, and just reply naturally.

03:31.900 --> 03:32.780
Yes, ma'am!

03:32.780 --> 03:35.150
What motivated you to study at our school?

03:35.150 --> 03:40.830
I suffered a serious illness when I was young, and I lost both my parents in an accident.

03:40.830 --> 03:43.080
But many people were still there to help me...

03:43.490 --> 03:45.710
All right, one last question.

03:45.710 --> 03:48.210
Do you have a future ambition?

03:49.170 --> 03:50.710
To bring world peace!

03:50.710 --> 03:52.090
Pardon?

03:52.090 --> 03:56.090
That's why I want to do something that involves helping others.

03:56.090 --> 03:57.260
Understood.

03:57.260 --> 03:58.800
This concludes the interview.

03:59.430 --> 04:01.140
Thank you very much.

04:02.720 --> 04:04.680
Congratulations on your enrollment,

04:04.680 --> 04:06.430
Nanakorobi Nene.

04:06.430 --> 04:10.610
May this school prove to be an asset for your future.

04:20.030 --> 04:21.240
What is it?

04:21.700 --> 04:22.830
Homework.

04:24.330 --> 04:26.290
I wanna!

04:26.290 --> 04:28.120
I wanna get inside BUER!

04:28.460 --> 04:33.340
I wanna see how Uzal solved this, and that, and everything else!

04:33.340 --> 04:36.130
I wanna! I wanna! I wanna!

04:37.590 --> 04:40.640
Anyway, Nene is my biggest obstacle right now.

04:45.890 --> 04:49.390
<i>She waltzes right through my
beefed-up security like it's nothing.</i>

04:52.560 --> 04:54.270
<i>A formidable foe.</i>

04:55.530 --> 04:58.900
<i>And it's all but impossible to get Nene alone, without the puppet.</i>

04:59.900 --> 05:03.660
<i>I'll have to distract them both to get anything done.</i>

05:04.330 --> 05:08.290
<i>What would distract Nene more than that damned puppet?</i>

05:08.290 --> 05:09.660
<i>A distraction...</i>

05:10.000 --> 05:11.540
That's it!

05:17.380 --> 05:22.050
I remade a retro game with
a modern engine that uses direct link!

05:23.680 --> 05:25.430
It's <i>Monster Bash 4</i>!

05:25.430 --> 05:28.060
Enjoy yourselves for the <i>entire</i> day, you hear!?

05:28.060 --> 05:30.230
Clarin, forward!

05:31.940 --> 05:36.400
Now I can mess with BUER all I want!

05:38.570 --> 05:40.950
<i>Th-That</i> didn't take long, did it?

05:40.950 --> 05:43.610
I wanted to play a little longer...

05:44.570 --> 05:48.910
Y-You shouldn't walk around carelessly with this thing!

05:48.910 --> 05:51.370
I'll keep a close eye on it for you—

05:51.370 --> 05:52.250
No.

05:58.460 --> 06:01.470
Darkness falls! Blinded, I've been!

06:01.470 --> 06:02.800
Mommy, I'm scared!

06:02.800 --> 06:05.510
There's a man with an axe under mine bed!

06:05.510 --> 06:07.220
Now there's no reason to worry.

06:40.420 --> 06:42.260
What gives?

06:42.260 --> 06:44.760
It's hard to get things done with you two staring at me.

06:44.760 --> 06:46.760
You don't have to stand watch.

06:46.760 --> 06:48.680
I won't try anything with BUER.

06:48.680 --> 06:50.010
Oh, sorry.

06:50.010 --> 06:52.520
It's actually homework for school.

06:52.520 --> 06:55.100
A report about work,

06:55.100 --> 06:59.570
with emphasis on how you felt as the job was being done, in order to...

07:01.440 --> 07:04.900
My line of work isn't a good example to learn off.

07:05.320 --> 07:08.530
I'll introduce you to a few businesses I'm affiliated with instead!

07:08.530 --> 07:11.990
Feel free to observe them instead, please!

07:11.990 --> 07:13.660
Thank you!

07:15.080 --> 07:17.500
Time to observe a few businesses!

07:18.080 --> 07:21.090
Are you keeping up with the
maintenance on your prosthetic body?

07:21.090 --> 07:22.630
Not a problem.

07:22.630 --> 07:24.420
Clarion will remind Nene.

07:24.420 --> 07:25.930
That's good to hear.

07:25.930 --> 07:27.930
Take care! See you later!

07:27.930 --> 07:29.930
See you later!

07:31.560 --> 07:34.850
So innocent. So trusting of others.

07:35.270 --> 07:37.440
Tricking her was a cinch.

07:40.270 --> 07:42.320
Schoolwork, huh...

07:42.320 --> 07:43.440
You don't want to do it?

07:43.440 --> 07:45.570
No, I look forward to it.

07:45.570 --> 07:49.870
I'm just wondering if this is
the right way to spend my time.

07:49.870 --> 07:50.950
The right way?

07:51.240 --> 07:52.950
Not too long ago

07:52.950 --> 07:56.540
I was helping out with research that would benefit mankind.

07:56.540 --> 08:01.340
I can't help but think that's a better use of my time than studying.

08:03.130 --> 08:05.630
If it's beneficial, it's worth installing.

08:05.630 --> 08:07.340
Do you need "study" installed?

08:07.340 --> 08:10.590
Do I need it <i>installed</i>?

08:13.430 --> 08:15.680
Well, if there's something I wanna do...

08:15.680 --> 08:18.980
having more knowledge certainly wouldn't hurt?

08:21.400 --> 08:25.480
If there's something you want to do,
just use the Pandora Device.

08:28.950 --> 08:31.820
I've helped out with things before,

08:31.820 --> 08:34.620
but I have no experience with work, full or part-time.

08:34.620 --> 08:37.410
Have you ever worked a job, Clarin?

08:37.410 --> 08:38.580
I'm doing so now.

08:39.370 --> 08:42.380
Being with Nene is Clarion's job.

08:43.460 --> 08:45.000
I'm not sure that really counts.

08:52.300 --> 08:55.430
Good morning, I'm Proserpina.

08:55.430 --> 08:57.730
I look forward to working with you today!

08:57.730 --> 08:59.020
Likewise.

08:59.560 --> 09:03.770
Since the terrorist attacks in Area Vulcan,
public order has taken a nosedive,

09:03.770 --> 09:07.780
and network disturbances have rendered the
infrastructure unstable here on Cenancle Island.

09:08.780 --> 09:11.780
Let's blow upsetting news like <i>that </i>right out of the water!

09:11.780 --> 09:14.160
How about something more extreme!?

09:14.160 --> 09:18.160
My entertainment career has resumed!

09:19.540 --> 09:22.000
The phoenix is reborn from the flames!

09:22.000 --> 09:24.500
I'll do something worthwhile to boost myself!

09:24.500 --> 09:28.050
Yes! A job is priceless!

09:28.050 --> 09:28.920
It's time!

09:28.920 --> 09:30.670
You got it!

09:30.670 --> 09:32.220
<i>I'm an idol!</i>

09:32.220 --> 09:34.350
I'm a reporter!

09:35.510 --> 09:37.770
<i>To work is magnificent!</i>

09:37.770 --> 09:39.640
<i>My name is Vli—</i>

09:51.360 --> 09:53.950
The first on Korobase's list.

09:53.950 --> 09:55.570
A hardware maker.

10:00.660 --> 10:04.790
Excuse me, I'm here to job shadow.

10:04.790 --> 10:08.420
Hello, and welcome to our company.

10:07.420 --> 10:09.210
Are they some big shot's daughters?

10:08.420 --> 10:11.760
We accept company tours all day.

10:09.210 --> 10:11.510
They sure have a wide range of prosthetics.

10:11.510 --> 10:12.760
Looks super expensive.

10:11.760 --> 10:15.930
Do you have an appointment?

10:12.760 --> 10:15.930
So cute! I've never seen girls like them before!

10:16.300 --> 10:20.430
I don't have an appointment, but I do have a reference.

10:27.230 --> 10:30.690
Welcome to our company, Miss Nanakorobi!

10:30.990 --> 10:34.950
Which floor might you wish
to see first, Miss Nanakorobi?

10:34.950 --> 10:37.030
Uh, well...

10:37.030 --> 10:42.450
We currently have a top-secret exoskeleton development lab you may find interesting!

10:42.450 --> 10:44.000
No, I'm just...

10:44.000 --> 10:45.040
No, no!

10:45.040 --> 10:49.340
Perhaps the young lady would be interested
in seeing our new line of artificial skin!

10:49.340 --> 10:52.550
Don't be afraid to ask if you wish to see anything, Miss Nanakorobi.

10:56.010 --> 10:58.390
Thank you for visiting our company!

10:58.390 --> 11:01.720
Please be sure to give our regards to Ms. Korobase!

11:01.720 --> 11:06.480
L-Let's see if we can avoid
attention at the next place, Clarin.

11:07.860 --> 11:11.230
Welcome to our company, Miss Nanakorobi!

11:11.230 --> 11:13.610
You may observe any floor of your choosing!

11:13.940 --> 11:18.410
This is the development lab for our
newly designed recoil-less handgun!

11:18.410 --> 11:21.790
Please let Ms. Korobase know we would be ever grateful if she financed our research

11:21.790 --> 11:24.620
into vibratory, gravity-controlling components.

11:24.910 --> 11:28.380
Our entire company welcomes you, Miss Nanakorobi!

11:28.750 --> 11:33.130
Come see the development of our new actuator
that links up with the latest cyborg OS!

11:33.510 --> 11:38.640
We would love for Ms. Korobase to license
her optronics patent to our company!

11:38.640 --> 11:39.760
Miss Nanakorobi!

11:39.760 --> 11:41.010
Let Ms. Korobase know!

11:41.010 --> 11:42.640
Miss Nanakorobi!

11:42.640 --> 11:43.890
Hurrah!

11:43.890 --> 11:45.890
Long live Ms. Korobase!

11:46.230 --> 11:50.650
Our company is confident that it can develop
high-resolution auditory components!

11:50.650 --> 11:54.740
This branch office deals with humane weaponry, primarily non-lethal ammunition!

11:53.110 --> 11:56.200
The cost to develop new components
and floating micro machines...

11:56.200 --> 11:58.360
...like to make some military connections!

11:58.360 --> 12:00.160
Please ask Ms. Korobase...

12:00.160 --> 12:01.240
...if Ms. Korobase would...

12:01.240 --> 12:02.240
Miss Nanakorobi!

12:02.240 --> 12:03.660
Please be sure to...

12:04.040 --> 12:06.250
Your face is stuck.

12:06.250 --> 12:07.410
Yeah...

12:12.420 --> 12:14.840
My face is finally back to normal.

12:14.840 --> 12:17.550
Did you gather the required
information for your homework?

12:19.130 --> 12:21.800
That wasn't exactly what I wanted to see.

12:22.260 --> 12:26.310
I just wanted to see people doing everyday work.

12:28.480 --> 12:30.270
Stop this!

12:30.270 --> 12:34.320
Get away from me!

12:31.940 --> 12:34.320
Scream all you like!

12:34.320 --> 12:36.940
Nene won't be back any time soon!

12:42.660 --> 12:46.290
The greatest! The mightiest! Titan TV!

13:16.480 --> 13:21.280
And so, for today's
Proserpina's Corner on <i>Cenancle-Wide,</i>

13:21.280 --> 13:26.660
we're coming to you from Vulcan Park,
where a bustling reconstruction event is underway!

13:26.660 --> 13:28.660
Wow, it's a TV person!

13:28.660 --> 13:30.080
I've never seen one before!

13:30.500 --> 13:31.370
Oh, I know!

13:31.370 --> 13:33.630
Okay, we've gone to commercial!

13:34.250 --> 13:36.340
Watch us work?

13:36.340 --> 13:37.380
Sure, I don't mind.

13:37.920 --> 13:39.470
Thank you!

13:41.090 --> 13:43.140
Nene and Clarin, huh?

13:43.470 --> 13:44.390
Clarion...

13:44.890 --> 13:47.010
This job is fun!

13:47.010 --> 13:49.890
But the pay isn't worth how chaotic it can get.

13:50.890 --> 13:52.020
But hey.

13:52.020 --> 13:56.770
It helps you advance your career by getting all sorts of new experience, and you get to meet stars.

13:56.770 --> 14:00.860
And most importantly, the hard work is rewarding.

14:06.410 --> 14:09.330
Money, gimme money!

14:09.330 --> 14:11.910
Pretty words don't put food on the table.

14:13.170 --> 14:14.420
It's a monster!

14:14.420 --> 14:16.420
Beat up the monster!

14:16.960 --> 14:21.300
Lookie here! Cenancle's popular
Mr. North is lively as ever today!

14:21.300 --> 14:25.800
Don't give some idol from the sticks her own TV segment!

14:27.680 --> 14:30.560
<i>Working a job sure seems tough.</i>

14:32.270 --> 14:35.650
Behind me, we have a tent set up to distribute food.

14:35.650 --> 14:38.570
It's relief aid for the disaster victims.

14:39.020 --> 14:40.530
How does it taste?

14:40.530 --> 14:42.150
It's very good.

14:42.150 --> 14:42.950
You know what?

14:42.950 --> 14:46.320
It tastes whole bunches better than Mommy's!

14:52.790 --> 14:57.080
If they're volunteers, that means they're working for no pay.

14:57.080 --> 14:59.960
It's one-sided aid, provided by individuals for nothing in return.

15:00.500 --> 15:04.840
If you consider a job to require or mean
"money changing hands," then this does not fit.

15:05.630 --> 15:09.470
But if you regard the entire island as a community,

15:09.470 --> 15:13.270
I suppose this is an economic activity that generates mutual benefit.

15:13.270 --> 15:15.310
<i>That</i> would fall under the definition of a job.

15:17.020 --> 15:20.270
I don't think they see it that way.

15:20.980 --> 15:23.530
It's more like, it's not about either side benefiting,

15:23.530 --> 15:26.740
it's about connecting with one-another.

15:27.110 --> 15:28.490
Connecting?

15:28.490 --> 15:29.620
With cables?

15:29.990 --> 15:31.080
No.

15:32.200 --> 15:33.620
A different way.

15:43.130 --> 15:44.340
Move it!

15:46.880 --> 15:49.390
C'mon, we told you to clear out!

15:50.760 --> 15:52.140
Hey, stop it!

15:52.140 --> 15:55.270
Who said ya could throw dis littl' shindig, eh!?

16:03.780 --> 16:05.740
P-Please, stop this!

16:05.740 --> 16:07.030
Get lost!

16:08.490 --> 16:13.200
E'ery day you you set up dees hotplates ya hurt our business, ya see!?

16:13.200 --> 16:14.160
Thas right!

16:15.410 --> 16:18.290
Quit eatin' this sorry shit!

16:28.090 --> 16:29.180
Clarin!

16:31.300 --> 16:32.970
'Sup with dis kid!?

16:32.970 --> 16:35.430
Got a problem with us, little girls!?

16:35.430 --> 16:37.060
Ye want some!?

16:39.900 --> 16:40.940
Clarin!

16:41.480 --> 16:42.310
You two...

16:42.310 --> 16:43.690
You're androids?

16:43.690 --> 16:47.070
Couple of lowly robots disobeyin' <i>humans</i>, their superiors!?

16:47.690 --> 16:50.070
Ow! The hell did that!?

16:50.490 --> 16:51.570
Stop it!

16:51.990 --> 16:54.200
Attacking young girls!? That's horrible!

16:55.200 --> 16:56.660
You stink!

16:57.330 --> 16:58.580
Ow!

16:58.580 --> 16:59.330
Shit!

16:59.580 --> 17:00.290
Sonuva...

17:00.290 --> 17:01.080
Goddammit!

17:05.300 --> 17:06.340
Hey, you guys!

17:06.670 --> 17:08.340
What's taking so long!?

17:08.340 --> 17:10.130
Oh! Boss!

17:10.130 --> 17:13.350
Things went all to hell thanks to them punks!

17:15.180 --> 17:16.350
Can we kick der asses?

17:16.350 --> 17:18.850
Retreat! Retreat! Retreat!

17:19.230 --> 17:22.350
Wha—!? Wait a minute,
why did we even bother to—

17:22.690 --> 17:25.940
<i>What's Sahar's puppet doing here!?</i>

17:25.940 --> 17:30.900
<i>Punks like these don't stand a chance
on their own against monsters like them!</i>

17:45.750 --> 17:48.380
Don't you at least have some emergency food?

17:48.800 --> 17:53.140
Thankfully the ingredients are safe,
but we're just amateurs.

17:53.680 --> 17:56.600
We wouldn't be able to re-prepare all this food on the spot.

17:56.600 --> 17:57.890
Oh, no...

17:58.220 --> 17:59.600
Let's go.

17:59.600 --> 18:01.890
I wanted to eat...

18:09.230 --> 18:11.860
Clarin... Please!

18:13.240 --> 18:15.490
Will you help me out again?

18:16.030 --> 18:19.040
Clarion's job is to assist Nene.

18:19.040 --> 18:20.250
Clarin...

18:24.500 --> 18:25.750
Thanks.

18:31.970 --> 18:34.760
Pandora Device, open!

18:46.440 --> 18:48.270
Sorry to keep you waiting!

18:50.360 --> 18:52.030
We're here to cook!

18:52.360 --> 18:53.070
Huh?

18:53.070 --> 18:56.160
But this is more than just two people can handle.

18:56.490 --> 18:57.780
No problem!

18:57.780 --> 18:59.160
Please let us help!

19:17.930 --> 19:20.720
Elpis Series, decode!

19:22.350 --> 19:24.060
Kitchen Drudge!

19:24.560 --> 19:26.810
W-Wow!

19:32.860 --> 19:37.820
D-Delicious!

19:56.090 --> 19:58.800
Well, thank goodness things worked out!

19:58.800 --> 20:01.810
We couldn't have done it without those cooks you brought.

20:01.810 --> 20:05.020
Huh? You mean you guys didn't call them?

20:07.020 --> 20:09.230
Thanks for looking after me today!

20:09.230 --> 20:10.940
You two!

20:10.940 --> 20:13.110
Hey, do you know where those cooks went?

20:13.110 --> 20:16.110
They said they had to leave on some urgent business.

20:16.110 --> 20:20.120
I see. I wish I could have thanked them properly.

20:20.120 --> 20:21.490
It's all right.

20:21.490 --> 20:24.950
I think the smiles everyone wore did that and more.

20:24.950 --> 20:26.290
I hope so...

20:26.290 --> 20:28.460
I would've liked to interview them too.

20:28.960 --> 20:32.250
Oh, yeah. Did this help you with your homework?

20:32.250 --> 20:33.630
It did!

20:33.630 --> 20:37.300
It helped me see that there are jobs that can put smiles on everyone's faces.

20:37.300 --> 20:39.510
And you were really cool!

20:44.310 --> 20:48.390
<i>I'm certain there was something connecting everyone today.</i>

21:01.110 --> 21:02.410
Colonel Kurtz.

21:02.410 --> 21:03.410
Talk.

21:03.410 --> 21:07.200
The plan to clear people out of the seaside park has failed.

21:08.000 --> 21:09.460
It matters not.

21:09.460 --> 21:11.750
It was never more than a consolation.

21:11.750 --> 21:16.170
The island's Self-Governance Organization
feels pressured not to get involved regardless.

21:16.670 --> 21:19.970
This causes not a second's delay to the schedule.

21:20.300 --> 21:24.930
As my watch ticks time away,
the inevitable fate of the island ticks with it.

21:33.940 --> 21:35.690
Just accept your fate!

21:46.950 --> 21:49.370
Y-Y-You two, again?

21:49.370 --> 21:52.080
Don't let it go to your puppet head!

21:52.080 --> 21:56.460
If I was even a <i>little</i> serious,
I'd reduce you to spare parts!

22:00.380 --> 22:01.510
Ah!

22:09.180 --> 22:12.480
Keep your hands off Clarin, <i>okay</i>?

22:12.850 --> 22:17.150
S-S-Sorry...

22:41.010 --> 22:44.010
Accessing the device named nature

22:44.010 --> 22:47.010
The circuit of infinite synapses

22:49.390 --> 22:52.770
Exchanging loops causes inevitable encounters

22:52.890 --> 22:54.730
You like that game, Nene?

22:53.480 --> 23:04.070
{talk}{this is pandoradio, it'll change each week, ignore this segemnt}

22:54.730 --> 22:56.150
You mean <i>Monster Bash</i>? Yeah!

22:56.150 --> 22:58.230
The quests are so great,
and there's tons of equipment to find!

22:58.230 --> 23:01.110
But I need rarer drops so I gotta play again and again and again

23:01.110 --> 23:03.990
and as I play I keep learning small new tricks and I enjoy the game so much and...

23:01.780 --> 23:03.990
You could have just said "yes."

23:04.070 --> 23:05.450
Saving data

23:05.450 --> 23:06.820
Strengthening predictions

23:06.820 --> 23:09.830
Even my latest updates

23:09.830 --> 23:15.120
can't help explain why you're so nice to me

23:15.120 --> 23:16.710
error error

23:16.710 --> 23:18.210
parameter

23:18.210 --> 23:21.550
Please help me understand

23:21.550 --> 23:23.720
where these emotions came from

23:23.720 --> 23:26.930
Find me at the end of this digital maze

23:26.930 --> 23:29.680
of feelings I can no longer control

23:29.680 --> 23:31.680
I understand the concept of emotions

23:31.680 --> 23:35.060
but I can't make any sense of my own

23:35.440 --> 23:38.060
I want to pull out these cords

23:38.400 --> 23:40.820
and head straight to you

23:40.820 --> 23:43.230
I won't come to understand love

23:43.230 --> 23:46.990
without having you here with me

23:52.330 --> 23:55.620
That's it! I want to investigate BUER's secret!

23:55.620 --> 23:58.880
Oh, maiden whose inner thighs
give shape to a beautiful triangle,

23:58.880 --> 24:00.790
I shall tell thee the secret of mine fifth leg.

24:00.790 --> 24:03.380
I was told to destroy you if you talk.
